title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › List › Open a patient or start a check
route: /authorizations/eligibility
intro: What a click on the list does. A row or its ID opens the result. 'Re-check' runs a check without leaving the list. 'Verify a patient' starts a new one.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "On the list, look at the patient rows"
screen sc "Patients table\nEach patient is two lines, both tint on hover, pointer cursor"

group gOpen "Open the result"
  click c1 "Click anywhere on a patient's two lines"
  click c2 "Click the patient ID, for example 'R-1042'"
  process p1 "Opens /authorizations/eligibility/R-1042\nThe browser Back button returns here with search and filters cleared"
endgroup

group gRe "Re-check in place"
  click c3 "Click 'Re-check' on a row"
  process p2 "The click stays on the row and does not open the result\nButton turns to a spinner and 'Checking'; the quiet second line says 'Checking now'"
endgroup

group gNew "A new patient"
  click c4 "Click 'Verify a patient' (top right)"
  process p3 "Opens /authorizations/eligibility/verify\nwith an empty form"
endgroup

screen res "Result page for that patient"
screen ver "Verify a patient\nEmpty form"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › What the page shows"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Re-verify a patient"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Fill in the form"
process t1 "About 1 second later the quiet line reads 'Checked just now'\nA toast reports the answer"

s1 --> sc
sc --> c1 & c2 & c3 & c4
c1 --> p1
c2 --> p1
p1 --> res --> g1
c3 --> p2 --> t1 --> g2
c4 --> p3 --> ver --> g3
